                            <comment id="14705633" author="cos" created="Thu, 20 Aug 2015 19:45:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The scenario you proposed is exactly what I did. I posted the fix on the email thread after the successful testing on the cluster. I think it&apos;d be a huge effort to test this in the Ignite, but having such an integration test in Bigtop would be relatively easy and  natural from the integration standpoint. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As for the reason behind it: with Ignite 1.3 a user has an ability to build and stand-up a Bigtop cluster with ignite-hadoop and spark in it and run spark-shell pointing to ignite-spark from an external repository. And it would work, except that indexing isn&apos;t there and if automatically pulled via spark-shell &quot;--packages&quot; cmd-option, it won&apos;t be available for the server nodes, where it needs to be. That&apos;s how we might get a non-working use-cases even without supplying ignite-spark as a part of Bigtop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, I&apos;d say let&apos;s have this fix in place that will at least address the immediate issue and then work on adding ignite-spark into Bigtop distribution. Thoughts?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14706431" author="iveselovskiy" created="Fri, 21 Aug 2015 09:03:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;As for now, I would suggest to commit the available patch as is (I believe, we already tested it enough), and have another ticket to include &apos;ignite-spark&apos; module into BigTop. When implementing it, we will revise again the possibility to add an integration test(s) for the Spark module.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14707463" author="cos" created="Fri, 21 Aug 2015 21:05:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks like a plan. Let&apos;s commit this and deal with the rest later.&lt;/p&gt;

